---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | Proof of Concept Bakery"
  description="What Proof of Concept Bakery receives, keeps and deletes, and when."
  screen="privacy"
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="draft">
    <strong>Draft:</strong> this page is published with the launch pull request.
  </p>

  <p class="lead" data-tour="privacy-lead">
    Every sandbox is deleted every night at 10:00 UTC, and Proof of Concept Bakery never asks for or
    stores your name, email, address or card.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare keeps deleted storage restorable for 30 days, so the account owner could bring rows
    back for a month. The bakery never restores a sandbox, and nothing in its code calls the
    restore.
  </p>

  <h2>What sign-in gives the bakery</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google:</strong> the bakery asks for <code>openid</code> only and receives an opaque
      identifier, <code>sub</code>. It keeps that only as a keyed hash. It receives no email, name
      or picture. Google’s consent screen still says the bakery will “Associate you with your
      personal info on Google”. That is Google’s fixed wording for the <code>openid</code> scope; we
      observed it on 2026-11-05 and the scope returns the identifier and nothing more.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>GitHub:</strong> the bakery reads the numeric user id from GitHub’s answer and
      discards the rest and the access token. It keeps the id only as a keyed hash.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A demo account:</strong> a generated username and a hash of the password you chose.
      There is no email, so there is no password reset: a forgotten password means a new account.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A guest:</strong> nothing but a cookie.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is kept, and for how long</h2>
  <div
    class="table-scroll"
    role="region"
    aria-label="Data the bakery keeps"
    tabindex="0"
    data-tour="privacy-table"
  >
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">What</th>
          <th scope="col">Kept for</th>
          <th scope="col">Why</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Session cookie</th>
          <td>24 hours, or until you sign out</td>
          <td>It lets you into your sandbox. The browser keeps it; page scripts cannot read it.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Sign-in transaction cookie</th>
          <td>10 minutes</td>
          <td>It holds the one-time values that make Google or GitHub sign-in safe.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">
            Account id (a keyed hash), and for a demo account the username and password hash
          </th>
          <td>Deleted 30 days after your last sign-in</td>
          <td>One sandbox across your devices.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Sandbox contents</th>
          <td>Until 10:00 UTC. A backstop deletes anything left after 36 hours.</td>
          <td>The demo itself. Its few free-text fields say they are wiped tonight.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Your IP address, as a hash with a salt that changes daily</th>
          <td>In logs for 7 days. The address itself is never stored or logged.</td>
          <td>Rate limits, daily caps and abuse review.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Country and continent</th>
          <td>In logs for 7 days</td>
          <td>Capacity and abuse review. Never a city, region or coordinates.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Turnstile’s signals</th>
          <td>Under Cloudflare’s policy</td>
          <td>It checks that you are a person when you make a sandbox or an account.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">That you turned “Under the hood” off</th>
          <td>In this browser tab, until you close it</td>
          <td>
            So the guide stays off as you move between pages. It is kept in the tab’s own storage
            and never sent anywhere.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Stripe sandbox objects, from the payments pull request (PR 5)</th>
          <td>Customers and drafts until the wipe; the rest until Stripe’s sandbox is reset</td>
          <td>Test payments. The details are synthetic.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 data-tour="privacy-wipe">What “Wipe now” does</h2>
  <p>
    It runs the night’s wipe for your sandbox alone, right away: the sandbox and everything it holds
    are deleted, and the bakery reports that to its own counter. The same 30 days of Cloudflare’s
    restore window apply, and the same promise: nobody restores it.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and consent</h2>
  <p>
    The session cookie is what lets the service you asked for work, so there is no consent banner.
    The bakery sets no cookie to track you and loads no third-party script, except Turnstile on the
    sign-in page.
  </p>

  <p class="asof">
    As of 2026-11-05. The detail is in the
    <a href="https://github.com/IHaveASegway/bakery/blob/main/docs/security.md">
      security document
    </a>
    .
  </p>
</Base>
